        "text": "Blood pressure should be mea­ sured at every routine clinical visit, or at least every 6 months. Individuals found to have elevated blood pressure with­ out a diagnosis of hypertension (systolic blood pressure 120–129 mmHg and diastolic blood pressure <80 mmHg) should have blood pressure confirmed using multiple readings, including meas­ urements on a separate day, to diag­ nose hypertension. A Hypertension is defined as a systolic blood pressure ≥130 mmHg or a diastolic blood pres­ sure ≥80 mmHg based on an average of two or more measurements obtained on two or more occasions. A Individuals with blood pressure ≥180/110 mmHg and cardiovascular disease could be di­ agnosed with hypertension at a single visit."
